    "lawCode": "Add §§230-e & 2805-z, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2113\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the public health law, in relation\nto requiring physicians and hospitals to obtain the name of the school\nattended by school-aged patients and to include this information in\ntheir admission registration forms\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill provides that hospital, medical clinics, and private\npractice physicians' offices include a request for the name of the\ncurrent school attendance of their patients.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would add a new section 230-e to the public health law, to\nrequire physicians to request and record the name and address of the\nschool attended by school-aged patients as part of the registration\nprocess and include that information in the patients' medical\nregistration form.\n\nThis bill would additionally add a new section 2805-2 to the public\nhealth law, to require hospitals and medical clinics to request, upon\ntreatment of patients who are currently enrolled in school, the name\nof the school that said patient attends and to include the same in the\npatient's records.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe death of 12 year-old Omar Rivera, who attended I.S. 211 in\nBrooklyn, from the methicillinresistant Staphylococcus aureus,\ncommonly known as MRSA, and the increasing number of reported infected\nstudents across the state, illustrates the need for health\npractitioners to be more responsive in alerting the affected community\nof their potential exposure to infectious diseases, and of immediate\npreventative.\n\nThis bill seeks to do just that, in a responsive, responsible way.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nUndetermined\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect one year after the date upon which it shall\nhave become law.\n",
